      "side": 1,
      "message": "(coding style)\n\nDon\u0027t do:\n\n```\nsourceVersion +\u003d 1\nextraFlags \u003d append(extraFlags, \"-target-version\", strconv.Itoa(sourceVersion))\n```\n\nDo:\n\n```\nextraFlags \u003d append(extraFlags, \"-target-version\", strconv.Itoa(sourceVersion + 1))\n```\n\nReason:\n\nDoing |sourceVersion +\u003d 1| doesn\u0027t make sense semantic wise. (So is the \"source version\" |sourceVersion| or |sourceVersion + 1| ?) |sourceVersion| sound like a constant, so it should be a constant. Initialize it, use it, and then recalculate it \u003d\u003e destroys it semantic.\n\nOTOH, \"append(extraFlags, \"-target-version\", strconv.Itoa(sourceVersion + 1))\" is much easier to read. \"|target version| is |source version| plus one\"",
      "revId": "2b44afb6a271b691ad9195b83590e55692a6a731",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
